 Every URL the build writes is relative, so the site works at a domain's root or in a folder.
 
+## Its pictures of the app
+
+Every screen of the app on the site (the stills in `assets/`, the frames in `assets/seq/` and the two plus videos) is shot from the real app, built against the e2e suites' mocked Supabase (`scripts/e2e/mock.cjs`) and seeded with a made-up coach's day (`tools/fixtures/db.cjs`: Niamh Byrne and her roster, Thursday 26 November 2026 at 11:20 am, the same people in every sport). When the app's look changes, remake them, one command a set, and look at them before they are committed:
+
+```
+export PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=$(npm root -g)/playwright        # as for scripts/e2e
+node website/tools/make.cjs all                           # every set, from a fresh mock build
+node website/tools/make.cjs stills --dist /tmp/nosca-site-mock                   # one set, from a build you made
+node website/tools/make.cjs stills --dist /tmp/nosca-site-mock --only home,peek  # some of the stills
+```
+
+| set | makes | with |
+|---|---|---|
+| `stills` | the stills: `coach-*`, `player-*`, `parent-family`, `junior-*`, `product-*` (the putting green in the clips), `partners-*` and `splash-*` | `tools/shoot.cjs` at 3x, then `tools/stills.py` (780 × 1688 WebP) |
+| `log` | `seq/log`: logging a lesson | `tools/seq/seq-log.cjs`, then `seq/seq-encode.py` |
+| `register` | `seq/register`: the register from the day | `seq/seq-register.cjs` |
+| `pt-register` | `seq/pt-register`: the clinic's register at 5:10 pm | `seq/seq-pt-register.cjs` |
+| `pd-feed`, `feed` | `seq/pd-feed` (the putting green) and `seq/feed` (the e2e suite's clip): a player's feed | `seq/seq-feed.cjs` |
+| `plus` | `motion-plus-golf.mp4`, `seq/plus/plus-scrub.mp4` and their posters | `tools/motion.cjs`, then `tools/motion-encode.py` |
+
+`--dist` is a mock build of the app (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://mock.supabase.co VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=mock VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=help@nosca.ie npx vite build --outDir /tmp/nosca-site-mock`); without it the tool makes one. It needs Playwright, Python 3 with Pillow, and ffmpeg for `plus`; the raw shots stay in `<tmp>/nosca-site-raw/<set>` to look at. The pages key their captions to frame numbers of the sequences (the marks in `seq/*/manifest.json`), so each sequence is asked for the same number of frames a segment every time (`make.cjs` holds the counts): a change to what a sequence shows is a change to the pages that play it. Each picture keeps the weight the site budgets for it (`stills.py` and `make.cjs` hold the qualities). The clip inside the screens is a putting green seen from above (`tools/fixtures/putting-green.webm`, cut from `assets/photo/loop-golf-green-1.mp4`), or the e2e suite's stylised ball flight for the stills and `feed` that always showed it.
+
 ## Its own address
 
 To give the site a domain of its own, add a second site in Netlify from this same repository with **Base directory** `website`, **Build command** `node build.mjs --out dist --release` and **Publish directory** `website/dist`, then point the domain at it. Nothing else changes.
@@ -36,12 +58,12 @@ To give the site a domain of its own, add a second site in Netlify from this sam
 - **The name.** Nosca is an anglicised spelling of the Irish word *nascadh*, which means linking (the founder, 23 November). On a page: "From the Irish *nascadh*, linking." Never "nasc" alone, and no other origin.
 - **Colour.** The business card is the art direction: its green, white, one quiet warm off-white, and gold only as a line, a numeral or small capitals. A sport's colour shows inside its own screen.
 - **Motion.** The scroll plays the page like a film, and it is never needed: with Reduce Motion on or JavaScript off every page shows whole and still.
-- **The screenshots are the app.** They are shot from the real build against demo data (the names are fictional) and re-shot when the app's look changes.
+- **The screenshots are the app.** They are shot from the real build against demo data (the names are fictional) and re-shot when the app's look changes (`tools/make.cjs`, above).
 
 ## What the founder can add
 
 - A contact email (`site.config.json`, `contactEmail`): Partners' close becomes "Partner with Nosca." with the address, and Home's close carries it, once it is there. While it is empty no address shows anywhere.
 - The story's first beat in his own words: when and where Nosca began, and why.
-- A real swing or forehand of his own, filmed with consent, for the clips inside the app's screens. They show a putting green seen from above today (a stock clip with no one to read as a customer); Story's plus sheet and register and Product's plus sheet are still shot from the app before 24 November's calmer keys, and want re-shooting from a build that has them.
+- A real swing or forehand of his own, filmed with consent, for the clips inside the app's screens. They show a putting green seen from above today (a stock clip with no one to read as a customer): his goes in as `tools/fixtures/putting-green.webm` (a WebM, since the browser that shoots them plays no H.264), and `make.cjs stills` and `make.cjs pd-feed` put it wherever the putting green is now.
 - His own photographs, if he would rather than the licensed ones (`assets/photo/`, the manifest says which picture stands where).
 - Partner marks, as they sign.
